<section class="section section--split c4-about" aria-labelledby="c4-about-title">
  <h2 id="c4-about-title" class="section__title">How the AI works</h2>
  <div class="c4-about__body">
    <p>The computer looks ahead at possible moves and replies, and assumes you'll play your best. Alpha-beta pruning skips lines that can't change its choice, trying center columns first makes that pruning work better, and a table of positions it has already searched saves repeating work. Easy and Medium only look a few moves ahead and add some randomness; Expert looks as far as it can in 2 seconds, usually 12 to 14 moves ahead.</p>
    <p>Expert is strong but not perfect, so it can be beaten. The <a href="https://github.com/SergioSimental/Connect4-AI">Java version</a> searches faster (18 to 32 moves ahead), and its Impossible level switches to a perfect solver from move 8, which never makes a mistake from there.</p>
    <p>It runs in a background thread, so the page never freezes while it thinks. It's a JavaScript port of the Java version, which also has a Monte Carlo Tree Search AI to compare against. The original was a <a href="https://github.com/AlexZ98/CS3520_Connect4">team project for CS 3520</a>.</p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/">← All projects</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
